Package: eyetrajectories
Title: R Interface for Functional Eye-Tracking Trajectories
Version: 0.4.1.9000
Authors@R: person("Stefanos", "Balaskas", email = "s.balaskas@ac.upatras.gr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides an experimental R interface to the Python package
    'eyetrajectoriespy' for continuous eye-tracking trajectory analysis.
    Provides a standalone native R core for common-grid trajectories,
    explicit preprocessing, quadrature-weighted dense FPCA and MFPCA,
    distances, kinematics, basic recurrence analysis and plots, alongside
    optional Python-backed advanced methods through reticulate. The native
    functionality requires no Python installation. Includes an experimental
    R-native sparse PACE adapter backed by 'fdapace', participant-level
    functional decomposition, cluster bootstrap diagnostics and discrete
    transfer entropy. Provides additional optional Python-backed wrappers
    for the 380 public Python functions recorded in the 2026-10-25 source
    snapshot, without implying native R parity. Research-only native
    extensions provide explicit landmark registration, delayed embeddings,
    binary recurrence network diagnostics and split-conformal anomaly screens.
